  "prediction": "**Summary of the Department of Defense's Foreign Currency Budget Rates and Management**\n\nThe Department of Defense (DOD) establishes foreign currency budget rates to determine its funding needs for overseas expenditures. These rates are used to calculate gains or losses due to foreign currency fluctuations. The report examines DOD's revised foreign currency budget rates since 2009 and their impact on projected Operation and Maintenance (O&M) and Military Personnel (MILPERS) funding needs.\n\n**Key Findings:**\n\n1. DOD revised its foreign currency budget rates in fiscal years 2014-2016, resulting in more closely aligned rates with those published by the U.S. Treasury Department (Treasury).\n2. The revised budget rates decreased DOD's projected O&M and MILPERS funding needs by $2.7 billion from fiscal years 2009-2017.\n3. DOD's use of revised budget rates resulted in a decrease in potential gains or losses due to foreign currency fluctuations.\n4. The Army's Foreign Currency Fluctuation Defense (O&M) reports are inaccurate and cannot be used to reliably track gains or losses.\n5. DOD lacks complete and accurate data to effectively manage the Foreign Currency Fluctuations, Defense (FCFD) account, which is used to cover losses due to foreign currency fluctuations.\n\n**Recommendations:**\n\n1. The Under Secretary of Defense (Comptroller) should conduct a review of foreign currency rates used at disbursement to determine cost-saving opportunities.\n2. The Under Secretary of Defense (Comptroller) should analyze realized and projected losses to determine the necessary size of the FCFD account balance.\n3. The Under Secretary of Defense (Comptroller) should revise the Financial Management Regulation to include guidance on ensuring complete and accurate data in Foreign Currency Fluctuation Defense (O&M) reports.\n4. The Secretary of the Army should develop a plan with timelines for implementing changes to its General Fund Enterprise Business System to accurately record disbursements.\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nDOD's revised foreign currency budget rates have improved the accuracy of its funding estimates and reduced potential gains or losses due to foreign currency fluctuations. However, DOD still faces challenges in managing the FCFD account and ensuring complete and accurate data. Implementing the recommended changes will help DOD better manage its foreign currency budget rates and reduce costs.",
